# Files the Vercel CLI must not upload.
#
# The CLI does NOT read .gitignore: it uploads everything in the folder except
# its own short default list (node_modules, .git, .next, .vercel, .env.local,
# .env.*.local, …) and whatever is named here. Git-ignored folders were being
# uploaded on every `vercel --prod` for that reason.
#
# Nothing below is read by `next build` or at runtime.

# The Expo app (docs/mobile/PLAN.md §5). Its own package, built by EAS, never by Vercel.
/mobile

# Source media kept beside the repo (see .gitignore) — tens of megabytes of video and
# brand originals that nothing in the app imports.
/marketing
/logo
/docs/reference
/Hornbill TapTap — Master Project Prompt.pdf

# Machine-local state and caches.
/.claude
/supabase/.temp
*.tsbuildinfo
/coverage

# Env files. Vercel injects the real values; .env.local is already excluded by
# default, and nothing should ride along by accident.
.env*
